      "description": "The function appends non-negative values to the store before checking for a negative value. If a negative value appears after some valid values, the store is partially mutated before the ValueError is raised, which contravenes the specification that the store must remain exactly unchanged when any negative value is present.",
      "evidence": "For example, calling append_batch([1], [2, -1]) results in the store becoming [1, 2] and then a ValueError, whereas the specification requires the store to stay [1]."
